      "page_title": "Trade-offs, Scaling and Interview Q&A",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Trade-offs",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Choice",
            "Pick A",
            "Pick B"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Per service",
              "Consistency: payment",
              "Availability: search"
            ],
            [
              "Tracking",
              "Push: smooth, live",
              "Pull: simple, 10 s lag"
            ],
            [
              "Dispatch",
              "Batching: fewer rides",
              "Speed: lower wait"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Scale reads and writes",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reads: CDN, Redis cache, read replicas, ==search shards== by city",
            "Writes: shard orders by `user_id`, location by `partner_id`",
            "Kafka topics partitioned by `order_id` keep per-order ordering"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Peak handling",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pre-scale before the 7-10 pm dinner peak",
            "Queue-based **load levelling** absorbs bursts",
            "Shed non-critical features like recommendations"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No ==idempotency== on payments: double charge on retry",
            "One shared DB across services: coupled schemas",
            "**Synchronous** call chain on the checkout path",
            "Ignoring thundering herds at peak: cache stampede, retry storms"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Outbox pattern",
          "text": "Write the event in the same DB transaction, then publish it. No commit, no event."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q1. How do you avoid assigning one order to two partners?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Atomic lock with `SET NX` and a TTL (~30 s)",
            "Winner assigns; idempotent write: same order, same partner",
            "Loser sees the lock taken and skips"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "SET lock:order:42 p7 NX EX 30"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q2. Payment succeeded but the order failed: what now?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Webhook **reconciliation** finds the paid, failed order",
            "Automatic **refund saga** returns the money",
            "Idempotency keys make each step safe to retry"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "INTERVIEW TAKEAWAY:",
          "text": "Shard writes, cache reads, isolate by city cell, and make every step idempotent."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "shield-check",
      "subtitle": "(Food Delivery App)"
    },
